   8: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   9:     """
  10:     Draw vertical bars for the colors whose bottom code-row frequency equals the marker count.
  11: 
  12:     Input structure
  13:     The grid has a dominant background, one solid full-width separator row, a
  14:     single contiguous marker run above the separator, and one non-background
  15:     code row below the separator.
  16: 
  17:     Rule
  18:     Count the marker pixels above the separator. In the code row, find every
  19:     color that appears exactly that many times. For each occurrence of such a
  20:     color, fill that column for the same number of cells immediately above the
  21:     separator, using the code-row color.
  22: 
  23:     Key insight
  24:     The marker run is the histogram target count, and the code row gives both
  25:     the colors to test and the columns where matching bars must be drawn.
